        q: `A group of subjects whose systemic blood pressure measurements are consistently between 145/95 mm Hg and 165/105 mm Hg is investigated for the cause of hypertension. They are found to have increased cardiac output and increased peripheral vascular resistance. Renal angiograms show no abnormal findings, and CT scans of the abdomen show no masses. Laboratory studies show normal levels of serum creatinine and urea nitrogen. Which of the following laboratory findings is most likely to be present in this group of subjects?`,
