        q: `In an autopsy study of apparently healthy young men between the ages of 20 and 25 years who died in motor vehicle accidents, elevated yellow streaks were found in the abdominal aorta. They were examined microscopically and biochemically to determine their cellular and chemical composition. Some lesions showed increased attachment of monocytes to endothelium. In others, foam-filled macrophages were found under the endothelium. Which of the following substances is most likely to be responsible for the transformation of macrophages into foam cells?`,
