        q: `A 59-year-old woman with type II diabetes mellitus experiences an episode of chest pain with exercise. On examination, her BMI is 30. Serum LDL cholesterol is 200mg/dl, and HDL is 30 mg/dl. Angiography reveals proximal coronary arterial narrowing with up to 70% stenosis. Which of the following pharmacologic agents ingested in low doses daily is most appropriate for reducing her risk for myocardial infarction?`,
