        q: `A 32-year-old woman has had coldness and numbness in her arms and decreased vision in the right eye for the past 5 months. On physical examination, she is afebrile. Her blood pressure is 100/70 mm Hg. Radial pulses are not palpable, but femoral pulses are strong. She has decreased sensation and cyanosis in her arms, but no warmth or swelling. Laboratory studies show serum glucose, 74 mg/dL; creatinine, 1 mg/dL; total serum cholesterol, 165 mg/dL; and a negative ANA test result. Her condition remains stable for the next year. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?`,
